      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The presenter says to go to the alarms page to see what it says: the tool changer is not in a safe position and recovery needs to be pressed.",
      "claim_ref": {
        "workflow_id": "REAL_WF_0003",
        "revision": 2,
        "entity_type": "claim",
        "entity_id": "REAL_WF_0003_CL_007"
      },
      "evidence_ids": [
        "REAL_WF_0003_EV_009"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The presenter says that pressing RECOVER gives the option to restore the tool changer or recover a tap; they press F1 to restore the tool changer, then press RESET, then press A to start automatic recovery.",
      "claim_ref": {
        "workflow_id": "REAL_WF_0003",
        "revision": 2,
        "entity_type": "claim",
        "entity_id": "REAL_WF_0003_CL_008"
      },
      "evidence_ids": [
        "REAL_WF_0003_EV_010"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "If automatic recovery does not succeed, the presenter says the machine kicks into manual recovery mode instead of completing the automatic path.",
      "claim_ref": {
        "workflow_id": "REAL_WF_0003",
        "revision": 2,
        "entity_type": "claim",
        "entity_id": "REAL_WF_0003_CL_036"
      },
      "evidence_ids": [
        "REAL_WF_0003_EV_016"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The presenter says that on an older machine, one is probably already familiar with manual recovery, and to press M to engage it.",
      "claim_ref": {
        "workflow_id": "REAL_WF_0003",
        "revision": 2,
        "entity_type": "claim",
        "entity_id": "REAL_WF_0003_CL_012"
      },
      "evidence_ids": [
        "REAL_WF_0003_EV_015"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The presenter says the on-screen notification tells them to remove all the tools, then rotate the arm in the reverse direction to its origin position.",
      "claim_ref": {
        "workflow_id": "REAL_WF_0003",
        "revision": 2,
        "entity_type": "claim",
        "entity_id": "REAL_WF_0003_CL_014"
      },
      "evidence_ids": [
        "REAL_WF_0003_EV_017"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The presenter says a tool can only be removed by depressing the plunger; otherwise it is really difficult and something is probably going to break.",
      "claim_ref": {
        "workflow_id": "REAL_WF_0003",
        "revision": 2,
        "entity_type": "claim",
        "entity_id": "REAL_WF_0003_CL_021"
      },
      "evidence_ids": [
        "REAL_WF_0003_EV_024"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The presenter says they continue rotating the arm until it reaches the origin position.",
      "claim_ref": {
        "workflow_id": "REAL_WF_0003",
        "revision": 2,
        "entity_type": "claim",
        "entity_id": "REAL_WF_0003_CL_022"
      },
      "evidence_ids": [
        "REAL_WF_0003_EV_025"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The presenter says the notification tells them the arm is at origin and asks them to raise the pocket up, which they do by pressing the up arrow.",
      "claim_ref": {
        "workflow_id": "REAL_WF_0003",
        "revision": 2,
        "entity_type": "claim",
        "entity_id": "REAL_WF_0003_CL_023"
      },
      "evidence_ids": [
        "REAL_WF_0003_EV_026"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The presenter says they like to check which tools were removed by going to the active tool window, pressing MDI; the window shows the two tools that were just in the arm.",
      "claim_ref": {
        "workflow_id": "REAL_WF_0003",
        "revision": 2,
        "entity_type": "claim",
        "entity_id": "REAL_WF_0003_CL_026"
      },
      "evidence_ids": [
        "REAL_WF_0003_EV_030"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The presenter says they can now update the tool table.",
      "claim_ref": {
        "workflow_id": "REAL_WF_0003",
        "revision": 2,
        "entity_type": "claim",
        "entity_id": "REAL_WF_0003_CL_027"
      },
      "evidence_ids": [
        "REAL_WF_0003_EV_031"
      ]
    }
  ]
}

