{
  "status": "answered",
  "statements": [
    {
      "text": "The first sign of trouble is either visual, such as rough tool change, or audible, such as an unusual sound or banging sound when the arm is loading or unloading a tool.",
      "claim_ref": {
        "workflow_id": "REAL_WF_0002",
        "revision": 2,
        "entity_type": "claim",
        "entity_id": "REAL_WF_0002_CL_002"
      },
      "evidence_ids": [
        "REAL_WF_0002_EV_002"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The presenter says to inspect the arms for dings, nicks and gouges on the alignment key and V shape of the arm.",
      "claim_ref": {
        "workflow_id": "REAL_WF_0002",
        "revision": 2,
        "entity_type": "claim",
        "entity_id": "REAL_WF_0002_CL_003"
      },
      "evidence_ids": [
        "REAL_WF_0002_EV_003"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The presenter says any of dings, nicks or gouges on the alignment key or V-shape indicate mis-loaded tools, a protruding set screw, or a tool-changer alignment issue.",
      "claim_ref": {
        "workflow_id": "REAL_WF_0002",
        "revision": 2,
        "entity_type": "claim",
        "entity_id": "REAL_WF_0002_CL_005"
      },
      "evidence_ids": [
        "REAL_WF_0002_EV_005"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The presenter says that in most cases, if the source of the problem is addressed, any damage can easily be fixed with a stone or a file and the double arm will not need to be replaced.",
      "claim_ref": {
        "workflow_id": "REAL_WF_0002",
        "revision": 2,
        "entity_type": "claim",
        "entity_id": "REAL_WF_0002_CL_006"
      },
      "evidence_ids": [
        "REAL_WF_0002_EV_006"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The presenter says excessive wear on the end of the double arm indicates the double arm height is set incorrectly.",
      "claim_ref": {
        "workflow_id": "REAL_WF_0002",
        "revision": 2,
        "entity_type": "claim",
        "entity_id": "REAL_WF_0002_CL_007"
      },
      "evidence_ids": [
        "REAL_WF_0002_EV_007"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The presenter says the double arm moving (raising or lowering) as it engages a tool is also an indication of an alignment or height problem.",
      "claim_ref": {
        "workflow_id": "REAL_WF_0002",
        "revision": 2,
        "entity_type": "claim",
        "entity_id": "REAL_WF_0002_CL_008"
      },
      "evidence_ids": [
        "REAL_WF_0002_EV_008"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The presenter says a separate video is dedicated to proper alignment and height-changing of the double arm.",
      "claim_ref": {
        "workflow_id": "REAL_WF_0002",
        "revision": 2,
        "entity_type": "claim",
        "entity_id": "REAL_WF_0002_CL_009"
      },
      "evidence_ids": [
        "REAL_WF_0002_EV_009"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The presenter says that in extreme cases, wear can cause tools to drop.",
      "claim_ref": {
        "workflow_id": "REAL_WF_0002",
        "revision": 2,
        "entity_type": "claim",
        "entity_id": "REAL_WF_0002_CL_010"
      },
      "evidence_ids": [
        "REAL_WF_0002_EV_010"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The presenter says the first place to look, if tools are dropping, is the tool changer locking mechanism (the finger).",
      "claim_ref": {
        "workflow_id": "REAL_WF_0002",
        "revision": 2,
        "entity_type": "claim",
        "entity_id": "REAL_WF_0002_CL_011"
      },
      "evidence_ids": [
        "REAL_WF_0002_EV_011"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The presenter says the finger should prevent the tool from being removed; while there may be a small amount of play, the tool should not be removable by hand.",
      "claim_ref": {
        "workflow_id": "REAL_WF_0002",
        "revision": 2,
        "entity_type": "claim",
        "entity_id": "REAL_WF_0002_CL_013"
      },
      "evidence_ids": [
        "REAL_WF_0002_EV_013"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The presenter says to press 5% rapid to slow things down, then command a tool change and press E-stop when the double arm is at the bottom of its travel.",
      "claim_ref": {
        "workflow_id": "REAL_WF_0002",
        "revision": 2,
        "entity_type": "claim",
        "entity_id": "REAL_WF_0002_CL_014"
      },
      "evidence_ids": [
        "REAL_WF_0002_EV_014"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The presenter says that with the tool in the arm and the arm in the down position, use a feeler gauge to check the gap between the finger and the V-flange of the tool holder.",
      "claim_ref": {
        "workflow_id": "REAL_WF_0002",
        "revision": 2,
        "entity_type": "claim",
        "entity_id": "REAL_WF_0002_CL_016"
      },
      "evidence_ids": [
        "REAL_WF_0002_EV_017"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The presenter says the clearance can be adjusted by changing the shim washers between the slide and the actuated arm.",
      "claim_ref": {
        "workflow_id": "REAL_WF_0002",
        "revision": 2,
        "entity_type": "claim",
        "entity_id": "REAL_WF_0002_CL_019"
      },
      "evidence_ids": [
        "REAL_WF_0002_EV_021"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The presenter says to also check the straightness of the arm, done simply with a straightedge.",
      "claim_ref": {
        "workflow_id": "REAL_WF_0002",
        "revision": 2,
        "entity_type": "claim",
        "entity_id": "REAL_WF_0002_CL_021"
      },
      "evidence_ids": [
        "REAL_WF_0002_EV_023"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "TG0128's Symptom Table lists three servo-related alarms for the double arm: 11.103 (TA-AXIS SERVO ERROR TOO LARGE), 11.108 (TA-AXIS SERVO OVERLOAD), and 11.994 (TA amplifier overload).",
      "claim_ref": {
        "workflow_id": "REAL_WF_0002",
        "revision": 2,
        "entity_type": "claim",
        "entity_id": "REAL_WF_0002_CL_024"
      },
      "evidence_ids": [
        "REAL_WF_0002_EV_026",
        "REAL_WF_0002_EV_027",
        "REAL_WF_0002_EV_028"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "TG0128 says any of these three alarms indicates the cambox is damaged, and directs testing the cambox per the guide's Cambox Test section.",
      "claim_ref": {
        "workflow_id": "REAL_WF_0002",
        "revision": 2,
        "entity_type": "claim",
        "entity_id": "REAL_WF_0002_CL_025"
      },
      "evidence_ids": [
        "REAL_WF_0002_EV_029"
      ]
    }
  ]
}

